{
  "comment": [
    "The table of the ownership summaries of spec/ownership-design.md 8: the order of the",
    "strongly connected components of the direct calls, the rounds and the work of a component,",
    "and the text form in src/fort/owner/summary.ft (8.1, 8.2); the interface hash, the summary",
    "file of the artifact and its reader in src/fort/library/artifact.ft (8.2, toolchain.md 2.2);",
    "--emit-summaries in src/fort/driver.ft; and the graph of a whole program in",
    "src/fort/gen_fir.ft. A decision `O8.n-<rule>` names the section of the design that owns the",
    "rule. Each row breaks one rule. The module suites compile the mutated module themselves; the",
    "build links the compiler so that the md5 guard reads it, and the second stage runs",
    "test/library/cache_test.py over that compiler, which holds a changed summary against the",
    "rebuild of each dependent. The table runs in the VM with the default runner after",
    "`tools/vm configure` and `tools/vm build`. The build waits 2 s and touches the sources in",
    "the guest first, as tools/mutations/artifact_fort.json does."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "src/fort/owner/summary.ft",
    "src/fort/library/artifact.ft",
    "src/fort/driver.ft",
    "src/fort/gen_fir.ft"
  ],
  "binary": "build/Linux/debug/fort",
  "build": "sleep 2 && touch src/fort/owner/summary.ft src/fort/library/artifact.ft src/fort/driver.ft src/fort/gen_fir.ft && cmake --build build/Linux/debug --target fort",
  "stages": [
    {
      "name": "the module suites of the summaries",
      "command": "python3 test/lang/run_tests.py --root test/fort --fort build/Linux/debug/fort --std-dir build/Linux/debug/std --verify-ir -j 4 owner/summary library/artifact gen_fir_summary driver_library driver_summary"
    },
    {
      "name": "the cache of the library builds",
      "command": "python3 test/library/cache_test.py --fort build/Linux/debug/fort --std-dir build/Linux/debug/std --cc clang --target x86_64-linux-gnu"
    }
  ],
  "mutations": [
